d  it's hard to explain  seeing him  with everything that he's accomplished  has been hard for him  but  he's doing it  he's not only a trained chef he's a  barista too  in fact he's added retail entrepreneur  to his resume with his own brand of  coffee i have  off my coffee what do you have  that new coffee this is for me yes well  thank you chris and  my girlfriend  and look what it says chris seen  limitless  chris without limits  he now made history earlier this year as  the first woman with down syndrome to  model for victoria's secret  secret i love it and she's also taken to  the catwalk at new york's fashion week i  love mother i love cameron you like the  camera yeah  i love camaron  thanks to the success of her modeling  career the 25 year old also has a deal  with the cosmetic giant l'oreal and she  is also building her own brand with the  support of her mother mimi she's working  on a fashion line tell me about this  little blessing in your life  she is a blessing she's a happy person  she brings joy to everyone do people  stop you because they recognize you see  yeah  yeah do they take a picture with you  yeah yeah  as a model and a businesswoman hidal  understands the importance of staying in  shape we were with her we saw she's in  the gym regularly five days a week doing  an hour every day you know she's also a  social media influencer she's got more  than six hundred thousand followers on  instagram  to see the two of them together is  really special  and although they live on opposite ends  of the island more than two hours away  from each other they have a standing  date it's a daily facetime call that  we're told can last up to three hours  just to be clear sophia you live in san  juan yeah i live in san juan puerto rico  and chris you live in rincon yes on the  western side of the island yes  yes they may be separated by distance  but when we were there we saw that they  are inspiring each other  living their best lives and continuing  to grow as individuals  following their dreams shattering  stereotypes and embracing success  and each other  they're setting an example for the rest  of us to live life  without limits  i could feel you building to that last  line without limits  i knew it was coming but i was going to  say it if you weren't going to say it  because they really personify that right  with the driver's license with the food  truck with all of their jobs it's an  amazing story look you and i both um  have ants right with special needs and  so i have a special place in my heart  for people who have special needs but in  fact they're simply just special people  and their ability to bring joy to other  people is what we wanted to share this  with also the parents you think about  this yes not setting the limit forget  defying expectations don't set the limit  don't set the limit you know dana chris  lives on his own found an apartment sort  of built it up sophia is still living  with her parents but i think the two of  them could live independently if they  wanted them to and their parents deserve  so much credit for setting them up like  that by the way chris turns 26 on friday  happy birthday buddy happy birthday  chris yeah redefining what it is to live  life without limits thank you that's a  beautiful story dave thank you very much  again thank you again
 

